    {
      "description": "Groups of one kind with its fixed measures, busiest first.\nkind: http, mcp (calls failed requests availability p50 p95 p99 users), job (runs failed p50 p95),\nspan (count p50 p95 p99), error (count lastSeen sample agcid), log, event (count),\nhost (cpu cpu_avg cpu_max mem disk load1 containers at), container (cpu cpu_avg cpu_max mem limit at).\nby: a comma list of extension, part, route, method, status, host, level, client, user_type, sub,\nversion (error adds type, container adds name). bucket 1m, 5m or 1h adds time as a group.\nsort: a measure or a by name; order desc or asc; nulls sort last. Same filters as logs__query.\nTests and services are left out of http and mcp unless user_type is given. Examples:\n- reliability per route, a day: {\"kind\":\"http\",\"by\":\"extension,part,route\",\"since\":\"24h\"}\n- worst availability first: {\"kind\":\"http\",\"by\":\"extension,route\",\"sort\":\"availability\",\"order\":\"asc\"}\n- tool calls per tool and client: {\"kind\":\"mcp\",\"by\":\"route,client\"}\n- errors by type, newest first: {\"kind\":\"error\",\"by\":\"type,extension\",\"sort\":\"lastSeen\"}\n- cpu of each machine in 5 minute steps: {\"kind\":\"host\",\"by\":\"host\",\"bucket\":\"5m\",\"since\":\"6h\"}\nmeta.nextCursor goes back as cursor for the next page. For the rows themselves use logs__query.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
        "properties": {
          "agcid": {
            "pattern": "^[0-9a-f]{32}$",
            "type": "string"
          },
          "bucket": {
            "enum": ["1m", "5m", "1h"],
            "type": "string"
          },
          "by": {
            "description": "comma list of group columns, e.g. \"route,status\"",
            "maxLength": 200,
            "type": "string"
          },
          "cursor": {
            "maxLength": 300,
            "type": "string"
          },
          "extension": {
            "maxLength": 64,
            "minLength": 1,
            "type": "string"
          },
          "host": {
            "pattern": "^(?!.*\\.\\.)[A-Za-z0-9][\\w.-]{0,252}$",
